Blackpool where 47 bands took part. Weeks holiday in New Brighton. Outings to Southport with Independent Order of Raccobites. Played cricket in nearby fields and later enjoyed dancing.	Sister was lame. Regular doses of liquorice powder. Wife had cancer.	Extensive information on running of household and childrearing and social class. Funeral horses had white reins for a child. Poor children got clothes from police and families would get a 4 pound loaf, tea, sugar and oatmeal from depots. On Sundays, RP and sister would go to soup kitchen, organised by a woman who liked having people around her. Father felt it was better to be away from relatives to escape their problems. Westhoughton Wakes - emblem of the Cowhead on ornaments and special pork pasties.	Interviewee's home	2	Farnworth	5	01.03.1970; 02.03.1970; 09.03.1970	Anne Burke	 	C707/104/1-2	1	1	43	2000int104	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
