nd sang solos in church. He could have gone to Canterbury Choir school on a scholarship but declined to do so.	Family liked singing and sang hymns while milking cattle. Father had series of sacred magazines. He used to go to cattle auctions with father. Annual two week holidays at Prestatyn when uncle took over farm. Friends always welcome. Mother went to Liverpool Scottish dance at St George's Hall. RW keen on football and went to a boy's gym at Massley Institute. Long walks and cricket.	Father had operation at home to prevent dizziness. Operated on by Sir Douglas Crawford and local doctor.	Extensive information on running of household, childrearing and social class.	Interviewee's home	3	Liverpool	5	18.03.1970	Audrey Hoskinson	 	C707/109/1-2	1	1	41	2000int109	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
