ther played the violin. Choir would come to the home at Christmas. Sunday school outings. Attended chapel concerts. After marriage, mainly socialised with husband's brothers and sister. Took local newspaper. Husband played football; belonged to working men's club. Attended church concerts.	EAL's son died in influenza epidemic in 1919 aged 5.	Father belonged to Odd Fellows Club. Interviewer's supplement to interview regarding EAL's domestic service.	Interviewee's home	1	Colchester	2	~	~	 	C707/129/1-2	1	1	56	2000int129	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
