and Sunday school. Chapel attending farmers rebelled against paying tithe to Anglican church.	Parents read and told stories. Parents had may friends. Father played billiards. RWP played mouthorgan (modulator). Father led singing in chapel. Parents played board games including chess. Books in the house, also The banner, The Nation, local paper, The Day. Went shooting with father. Days out on Bank Holidays to Llanaber and Barmouth. Sang alto in Idris choir. RWP liked to tend sheep and ride. He had a dog. Went fishing; walked in the mountains.	~	Family grew own fruit and vegetables and kept hens. Very neighbourly valley. Emergencies were indicated to neighbours by placing a white cloth on a designated bramble or holly plant. RWP heard Tudor Davis and Madam Norah Even Williams sing.	Interviewee's home	1	Ffestinog	10	~	~	 	C707/130/1	1	1	46	2000int130	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	1	Open reel	1	2	1	1
