ngs to Southend. Children stayed for a month in the summer holidays with relatives in Kirby. Went to Lismore Circus to play. Family played card games. Visits to concerts and cinema.	Father had to give up work because of illness. Two sisters died of TB.	Family's clothes made by dressmaker. Father had an allotment. Father kept a horse and dogs for his business. Cats as pets. Rabbits were sent by rail from relatives living in the country. Christmas was celebrated. Sunday school outings to Epping. OH bought insurance stamps as self-employed person when working for own family. Aware of insecurity of unskilled labour; class differences; poverty.	Interviewee's home	3	London	3	19.06.1970	Lena Ingers	 	C707/133/1-3	1	1	76	2000int133	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	3	Open reel	1	2	1	1
