olton. Mother and father would go to the cinema together. Mother went to Mothers Union. WB cycled, walked; fished (in canal); played football.	Mother was deaf. In later life she had a bad heart.	Mother had help with washing. Mother knitted some children's clothes including stockings. Eldest sister was a manageress of Morris's shoe shop. Grandmother had a shop and owned a house. Family kept a dog. WB taught to show respect by raising cap to elders. Family insurance for children; father belonged to Oddfellows. Family kept hens also had two cocks for eating at Christmas and New year. Comprehensive interview. Details of family clothing; family life; family meals; children's games; differences in church denominations; social mobility.	Interviewee's home	2	Bolton	5	19.02.1970	Thelma Crook	 	C707/134/1-3	1	1	75	2000int134	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	2	2	1	1
