reasurer for the Bolton United Harriers. Mother liked to go to Isle of Man for holidays. Mr L and wife holiday on Isle of Man for 40 years. New Year was celebrated. Went to annual circus.	Fourth child, sister, died aged 14.	Police, when stolen goods brought to pawnshop. Father owned properties. Mother's family had kept the Bull in Badgergate pub. Second brother was killed in World War I. Family paid insurance. Aware of class division. Saw much hardship and poverty. Family considered itself middle-class. Report of interview by interviewer.	Interviewee's home	2	Bolton	5	06.07.1970; 08.07.1970	Anne Burke	 	C707/137/1-2	1	1	80	2000int137	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
