 war.	Parents and children did not attend church but were not atheists.	Father told children stories and took them for walks. Father played the zither. Sisters played violin and piano. Family sang and played game. Family had party at Christmas. Family took newspapers and magazines. Holidays to mother's relatives in Much Wellock, Shropshire. Father took long walks to Halifax zoo and Likely Moore. FS very interested in natural history and collected caterpillars. Joined YMCA aged 19 years.	~	Mother made sisters' clothes. FS and father had clothes made by bespoke tailor. Mother made wine. Parents belonged to Co-operative savings club and sick club. Little Brief Funeral Club at Ingrow Wesley Place Sunday School. Keighley society divided into rich manufacturing, owners of engineering works, crafts and labouring, mill workers. Aware of poverty and wealth in Keighley community, class distinction, distinction between skilled and unskilled work.	Interviewee's home	2	Keighley	9	16.09.1970	Ann Cryer	 	C707/146/1-2	1	1	76	2000int146	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
