 Brighton races. Husband was football trainer for his work. Kept cats.	One twin died in infancy. Mother had bad legs. Father was injured by a horse.	Father grew flowers, kept chickens, rabbits and pigeons. Mother cooked on a penny-in-the-slot gas stove. Parents paid into Christmas club, drapery club, and insurance; also holiday fund. Books from Buttercup Library. Went to Wells in Norfolk. Details of pub benefits; children's games; class; drunken fighting.	Interviewee's home	3	London	3	12.03.1971	~	 	C707/197/1-2	1	1	79	2000int197	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
