njoyed cinema and theatre.	Husband died in 1927 after being kicked by a horse.	Grandfather served three months for hitting policeman. Was unwanted child. Father was killed at Phoenix Park. Grandparents had birthday parties for the girls and themselves. Grandmother kept bantam hens. Grandfather had pony and trap, wore top hat, tails and kid gloves. Aware of differences between religious denominations, and social class. Considered grandparents as middle-class. AN spoke Gaelic	Interviewee's home	2	Stoke-on-Trent	8	24.05.1971; 25.05.1971	Carol Holder	 	C707/202/1-2	1	1	58	2000int202	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
