ngham during school holidays, sometimes at Christmas. Father and mother sometimes went to Grand Theatre music hall. Enjoyed country walks and cycling. Played football and later joined tennis club. Later enjoyed cycling, sprinting. Late-teens became interested in theatre, particularly Gilbert and Sullivan.	Was affected by benzene fumes while at British Celanese.	Grandfather was a Haslam, overseas freezer transport. Grandfather was very interested in natural history, fostered the interest in his grandsons. Helped father in the garden. Family bought at Co-operative shops. Family kept hens and goats, and grandfather kept pigeons. Family took Daily Citizen. Comprehensive interview. Detail: grandfather Haslam; father's employment and unemployment; pawn broking; politics; James Thomas; local community; schooling; Rolls Royce.	Interviewee's home	2	Derby	1	06.04.1971; 15.04.1971	Jean Jacobs	 	C707/221/1-2	1	1	64	2000int221	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
