 class; walked and rambled with the music class. Attended symphony and choral concerts. Was friend of Reginald Mantel.	Father was a semi-invalid for some years but continued to work. GFC had tuberculosis in 1936. Was in Loggerheads sanatorium for 12 months.	Mother had help with housework from time to time. Mother made some of the family's clothes. Bought shoes from Saunders in London Road. Father helped in the home. Father look after Flemish refugees during World War I. Went with mother to market on Saturday evenings. Family considered lower middle-class. Detail: Sir Lawrence Stainer; social status; secondary school teachers; the Front; Coronation of Edward VII.	Interviewee's home	2	Stoke-on-Trent	8	??.04.1971	Carroll Hill	 	C707/224/1-2	1	1	72	2000int224	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
