ather repaired shoes. Mother sewed and knitted. Clothes were bought from CWS in Shilton and Bishop Auckland. Father helped in the home when mother was confined. Mother paid into sick club. Employer's son owned a mill. Employers had private means. Employer made bread and jam. Home had many books and newspapers. Belonged to a Library.	Interviewee's home	2	Darlington	4	12.06.19; 14.06.1971	Doris Redfern	 	C707/226/1-2	1	1	76	2000int226	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
