thorpe. Parent's friends fame to house to play billiards. Collected picture postcards. When older, enjoyed going to the cinema, cycling and walking with friends. Was not allowed to go dancing.	Mother died giving birth to MW. Father had a congloctomy operation. MW had a very bad stammer.	Family had live-in maid. When children were born, had extra domestic help for a month. Until aged two to three years, MW was looked after by relatives and carers until father remarried. Father kept pigeons. Children had pet rabbits. Did not know for many years that mother was actually stepmother. Detail: treatment at school; Bridgford community young men came from France to learn lace trade and English	Interviewee's home	2	Eastwood	1	01.02.1971; 04.02.1971; 22.02.1971	Dennis Pettitt	 	C707/227/1-2	1	1	55	2000int227	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
