bought Girls Friend. Mother read to the children. Mother took children to visit relations. Sunday school outings to Spittal. Stayed with an aunt in Alnwick. Visited grandparents twice a year. Attended village concerts. Father went to the pub every evening. Belonged to the Girls Friendly society.	Mother died of consumption (tuberculosis). ES was a sickly child.	Mother was a good housekeeper, baked bread. Mother would knit, crochet and sew. Father helped in the house, took children for walks, and told children stories. Shopping was done in Berwick. Parents grew vegetables, kept a pig and hens. Parents paid into sick club. The Little's followed hounds. Mrs Little was the daughter of Sir John Usher. Comprehensive interview. Details: salmon fishing; home baking and family meals; children's games; village of Norham; employers' households; life in service; estate farm.	Interviewee's home	1	Darlington	2	01.04.1971; 27.04.1971; 04.05.1971	Doris Redfern	 	C707/231/1-3	1	1	117	2000int231	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	3	Open reel	1	2	1	1
