vative. SM apolitical.	Attention Church of England Sunday school. Sons attended Sunday school and Bank of Hope.	Visited home every two years. Had friends to tea on birthdays. Mother, and later SM, sang with the Messiah Choir. Aunt and uncle to SM to the Palace of Varieties and to magic lantern shows. Bank holiday outings to Southend, Hern Bay or Upnor. Sunday school outings to cherry farm. Went hop picking. Later went dancing with sister and friends. SM and husband played Ludo and dominoes with sons, read to them, and took them to the cinema. Had short holidays in Cleethorpes.	Husband died as a result of a car accident caused by employer's drunken diving.	SM was not happy living with aunt and uncle. Although affectionate, uncle was strict, aunt punished frequently. While schoolgirl, took uncle's food to him at work at the Chatham Dockyard. Detail of working at Eriksons; siblings' careers.	Interviewee's home	2	Beeston	1	28.09.1971; 30.09.1971	Dennis Pettitt	 	C707/243/1-2	1	1	96	2000int243	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
