ater the piano. Went to Sunday school outings to the country. Joined the Boys Brigade and gymnasium. Wrestled, middle-weight, in Olympics of 1928 and 1932. When older, enjoyed swimming at Highgate Pond, going to the cinema and variety shows.	Young brother died in infancy.	Mother belonged to Mothers Union. Belongings were often pawned. Father drank. Marie Stopes clinic opened opposite where family lived. Childless couple in same house cared for and fed the children, particularly JM. JM had to look after sisters while parents went out to the cinema. Parents paid into slate club at pub. Details: employers; religion; local community; police.	Interviewee's home	3	London	3	02.03.1971; 26.03.1971	~	 	C707/245/1-2	1	1	69	2000int245	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
