ish. Mother kept hens for a short time. Children had to pick coal three times a day. Christmas was celebrated with small presents and special food. Father bet on horses. Neighbours helped when there was illness or at child birth. Father and mother argued. Had help from the Parish. Some detail of poor working-class neighbourhood; employment conditions; police; street gambling; rent.	Interviewee's home	2	Stoke-on-Trent	8	30.07.1971; 09.08.1971; 12.08.1971	Carol Holder	 	C707/248/1-2	1	1	57	2000int248	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
