ometimes took the children for walks. Brothers went to camp with the church. First holiday for RN was when aged 11-12 years, was a visit to an aunt in Ashbourne, Leek, was made to look after five cousins. Sunday school outings to Shooters Hill, Cromwells Caves and Rudyard. Went to musical halls at Longton theatre. When older, went to cinema with sister and girlfriend.	Father had lumbago.	Clothes were bought from Martins, shoes from Craddocks. Older sister helped in the home. RN baked from a young age. Mother baked bread and made jams. Took father's mid-day meal to his work. Father was a jealous man, and moody; left home when RN was aged 13-14.	Interviewee's home	2	Stoke-on-Trent	8	??.05.1971	Carroll Hill	 	C707/251/1-2	1	1	68	2000int251	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
