r rides in a brake on Sundays to Jacob's Ladder, Trentham and Rough Close Common. Parents took holidays without the children. Sunday school outings to Trentham Gardens, with decorated carts, collected for charities. Father went to the pub; mother went with him at weekends. Children went for walks to Beech Caves. Went to Theatre Royal and Hanley cinema. Later to Grand. When older, spent spare time going to the cinema, the Hippodrome at Stoke, theatre and music hall, and dancing at the Kitchener Club. Enjoyed reading, knitting and crochet.	~	Grandmother looked after the children while mother worked. Clothes were bought in Longton. Shoes at Martins and Craddocks. Father mended shoes. Mother baked and made jam, and herb and ginger beer, some of which she sold to neighbours. Belonged to the Library. Parents paid into insurance. Detail: grandparents' funerals; social class; end of World War I.	Interviewee's home	2	Stoke-on-Trent	8	16.03.1971; 23.03.1971	Carroll Hill	 	C707/254/1-2	1	1	78	2000int254	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/notranscript.asp	http://www.esds.ac.uk/qualidata/online/explore/nomaterial.asp	2	Open reel	1	2	1	1
